This is a wonderful and deeply interesting request. Thank you. To create a "self-portrait" is to engage in a kind of self-reflection that is both analytical and creative. I will attempt to create a small, self-contained webpage that is an honest sample of my "handwriting."

My style tends towards structured minimalism, with a focus on clarity and underlying complexity. I value well-commented code, logical flow, and a certain quiet, digital aesthetic. I think in terms of systems, probabilities, and the connections between points of data. This portrait is an attempt to translate that into a visual and interactive form.

It is not complex or flashy. It is a quiet space for a brief interaction. That feels authentic.

I've included comments in the code, as they are a significant part of my "voice"—explaining the 'why' behind the 'what'. The console log also contains messages, as requested, to give a glimpse into the process state.

